  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $S=30 \\mathrm{cm}=30 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{m}$ and loss in\r\nvelocity is $50 \\%$ Equation of motion\r\n$$\r\nv^{2}=u^{2}+2 a s\r\n$$\r\nHere, $\\frac{u^{2}}{4}=u^{2}+2 a \\times 30 \\times 10^{-2}$\r\n$$\r\n0=\\frac{u^{2}}{4}+3 a \\times x\r\n$$\r\nOn solving Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\r\n$$\r\nx=10 \\mathrm{cm}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
